-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 102(a) (piece dg1): what the certificate of
-- incorporation shall set forth. Layer 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
-- Subsections (b) to (d) and (f) are in dg1-s102b-optional-provisions.l4, subsection (e) (reserving a name) in
-- dg1-s102e-name-reservation.l4.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- The Division of Corporations in the Department of State and the Secretary of State are officials: no seat.
-- A waiver or finding the text leaves to them is an input (`the Division of Corporations waives the
-- requirement`, `the Division determines ...`), never computed.

§ `Section 102(a) -- What the certificate of incorporation shall set forth`

§§ `s 102(a)(1) The name`

-- Limb (i): the name shall contain one of twelve words, or an abbreviation of one (with or without punctuation),
-- or words of like import of foreign countries or jurisdictions written in roman characters or letters. The
-- twelve words are carried as data so that a seat can list them.
-- src:42 | (1) The name of the corporation, which (i) shall contain 1 of the words “association,” “company,” “corporation,” “club,” “foundation,” “fund,” “incorporated,” “institute,” “society,” “union,” “syndicate,” or “limited,” (or abbreviations thereof, with or without punctuation), or words (or abbreviations thereof, with or without punctuation) of like import of foreign countries or jurisdictions (provided they are written in roman characters or letters); …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(1)(i) (src:42)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 102(a)(1)(i) the words one of which the name must contain` MEANS
    LIST "association", "company", "corporation", "club", "foundation", "fund", "incorporated", "institute", "society", "union", "syndicate", "limited"

-- src:42 | (1) The name of the corporation, which (i) shall contain 1 of the words “association,” “company,” “corporation,” “club,” “foundation,” “fund,” “incorporated,” “institute,” “society,” “union,” “syndicate,” or “limited,” (or abbreviations thereof, with or without punctuation), or words (or abbreviations thereof, with or without punctuation) of like import of foreign countries or jurisdictions (provided they are written in roman characters or letters); …
-- src:42 | provided, however, that the Division of Corporations in the Department of State may waive such requirement (unless it determines that such name is, or might otherwise appear to be, that of a natural person) if such corporation executes, acknowledges and files with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 of this title a certificate stating that its total assets, as defined in § 503(i) of this title, are not less than $10,000,000, or, in the sole discretion of the Division of Corporations in the Department of State, if the corporation is both a nonprofit nonstock corporation and an association of professionals, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(1)(i) (src:42)
DECLARE `s 102(a)(1)(i) Name words` HAS
    `the name contains one of the listed words or an abbreviation of one, with or without punctuation`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name contains words of like import of foreign countries or jurisdictions, written in roman characters or letters` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 a certificate stating its total assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total assets the certificate states, as defined in § 503(i) of this title, in dollars`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the Division determines that the name is, or might otherwise appear to be, that of a natural person`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation is an association of professionals`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Division of Corporations waives the requirement`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- The Division may waive the requirement (unless it determines that the name is, or might otherwise appear to be,
-- that of a natural person: read as limiting both routes, see the Fork register) if the corporation files a
-- certificate stating total assets of not less than $10,000,000, or, in the Division's sole discretion, if the
-- corporation is both a nonprofit nonstock corporation and an association of professionals. Total assets are
-- "as defined in § 503(i)" (8 Del. C. ch. 5, not among the inputs): the stated amount is an input.
-- src:42 | provided, however, that the Division of Corporations in the Department of State may waive such requirement (unless it determines that such name is, or might otherwise appear to be, that of a natural person) if such corporation executes, acknowledges and files with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 of this title a certificate stating that its total assets, as defined in § 503(i) of this title, are not less than $10,000,000, or, in the sole discretion of the Division of Corporations in the Department of State, if the corporation is both a nonprofit nonstock corporation and an association of professionals, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(1)(i) (src:42)
GIVEN name IS A `s 102(a)(1)(i) Name words`
      kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(1)(i) the name satisfies the requirement as to words` name kind MEANS
        name's `the name contains one of the listed words or an abbreviation of one, with or without punctuation`
     OR name's `the name contains words of like import of foreign countries or jurisdictions, written in roman characters or letters`
     OR (    name's `the Division of Corporations waives the requirement`
         AND (NOT (name's `the Division determines that the name is, or might otherwise appear to be, that of a natural person`))
         AND (   (    name's `the corporation executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 a certificate stating its total assets`
                  AND (name's `the total assets the certificate states, as defined in § 503(i) of this title, in dollars` AT LEAST 10_000_000))
              OR (    `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind
                  AND name's `the corporation is an association of professionals`)))

