`s 102(a)(2) the certificate sets forth the registered office and registered agent` stated MEANS
    -- out of range: section 131(c) (piece dg2) says how an address is stated
        stated's `the certificate states the address of the corporation's registered office in this State`
    AND stated's `that address is stated in accordance with § 131(c)`
    AND stated's `the certificate states the name of the corporation's registered agent at that address`

§§ `s 102(a)(3) The business or purposes`

-- It is sufficient to state, alone or with others, that the purpose is to engage in any lawful act or activity for
-- which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware.
-- src:44 | (3) The nature of the business or purposes to be conducted or promoted. It shall be sufficient to state, either alone or with other businesses or purposes, that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware, and by such statement all lawful acts and activities shall be within the purposes of the corporation, except for express limitations, if any;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(3) (src:44)
GIVEN `the certificate states the nature of the business or purposes to be conducted or promoted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(3) the certificate sets forth the nature of the business or purposes` `the certificate states the nature of the business or purposes to be conducted or promoted` `the certificate states that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware` MEANS
        `the certificate states the nature of the business or purposes to be conducted or promoted`
     OR `the certificate states that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware`

-- By that statement all lawful acts and activities are within the purposes, except for express limitations, if any.
-- If the certificate states only particular purposes, whether an act is within them is not decided here (NOTHING).
-- src:44 | that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware, and by such statement all lawful acts and activities shall be within the purposes of the corporation, except for express limitations, if …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(3) (src:44)
GIVEN `the certificate states that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or activity is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains an express limitation that excludes the act or activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(3) the act or activity is within the purposes of the corporation` `the certificate states that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware` `the act or activity is lawful` `the certificate contains an express limitation that excludes the act or activity` MEANS
    IF `the certificate states that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware`
    THEN JUST (`the act or activity is lawful` AND (NOT (`the certificate contains an express limitation that excludes the act or activity`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 102(a)(4) Stock, or the nature of a nonstock corporation`

-- A corporation that is to be authorized to issue stock.
-- src:45 | (4) If the corporation is to be authorized to issue only 1 class of stock, the total number of shares of stock which the corporation shall have authority to issue and the par value of each of such shares, or a statement that all such shares are to be without par …
-- src:45 | If the corporation is to be authorized to issue more than 1 class of stock, the certificate of incorporation shall set forth the total number of shares of all classes of stock which the corporation shall have authority to issue and the number of shares of each class and shall specify each class the shares of which are to be without par value and each class the shares of which are to have par value and the par value of the shares of each such …
-- src:45 | The certificate of incorporation shall also set forth a statement of the designations and the powers, preferences and rights, and the qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, which are permitted by § 151 of this title in respect of any class or classes of stock or any series of any class of stock of the corporation and the fixing of which by the certificate of incorporation is desired, and an express grant of such authority as it may then be desired to grant to the board of directors to fix by resolution or resolutions any thereof that may be desired but which shall not be fixed by the certificate of incorporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
DECLARE `s 102(a)(4) Authorized stock stated` HAS
    `the number of classes of stock the corporation is to be authorized to issue`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the certificate states the total number of shares of stock which the corporation has authority to issue`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states the par value of each of the shares, or that all the shares are to be without par value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states the number of shares of each class`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate specifies each class the shares of which are to be without par value, each class the shares of which are to have par value, and the par value of the shares of each class with par value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incorporators desire to fix by the certificate the designations, powers, preferences and rights, and qualifications, limitations or restrictions, permitted by § 151 for a class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets forth a statement of them`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incorporators desire to grant the board of directors authority to fix by resolution any of them not fixed by the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets forth an express grant of that authority`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- One class: the total number of shares and the par value of each (or that all are without par value). More than
-- one class: the total number of shares of all classes, the number of each class, and which classes have par
-- value and what it is. Also, to the extent desired: the statement of the rights of any class or series that the
-- certificate fixes (section 151, piece dg3), and the express grant of authority to the board to fix by
-- resolution those that it does not fix. Fewer than one class, or a fractional number of classes, is not covered.
-- src:45 | (4) If the corporation is to be authorized to issue only 1 class of stock, the total number of shares of stock which the corporation shall have authority to issue and the par value of each of such shares, or a statement that all such shares are to be without par …
-- src:45 | If the corporation is to be authorized to issue more than 1 class of stock, the certificate of incorporation shall set forth the total number of shares of all classes of stock which the corporation shall have authority to issue and the number of shares of each class and shall specify each class the shares of which are to be without par value and each class the shares of which are to have par value and the par value of the shares of each such …
-- src:45 | The certificate of incorporation shall also set forth a statement of the designations and the powers, preferences and rights, and the qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, which are permitted by § 151 of this title in respect of any class or classes of stock or any series of any class of stock of the corporation and the fixing of which by the certificate of incorporation is desired, and an express grant of such authority as it may then be desired to grant to the board of directors to fix by resolution or resolutions any thereof that may be desired but which shall not be fixed by the certificate of incorporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
GIVEN stock IS A `s 102(a)(4) Authorized stock stated`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(4) the certificate sets forth the authorized stock` stock MEANS
    -- out of range: section 151 (piece dg3) decides what rights, preferences and limitations may be fixed
    IF (stock's `the number of classes of stock the corporation is to be authorized to issue` LESS THAN 1)
       OR (NOT (FLOOR (stock's `the number of classes of stock the corporation is to be authorized to issue`) EQUALS stock's `the number of classes of stock the corporation is to be authorized to issue`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (
            (IF stock's `the number of classes of stock the corporation is to be authorized to issue` EQUALS 1
             THEN (    stock's `the certificate states the total number of shares of stock which the corporation has authority to issue`
                   AND stock's `the certificate states the par value of each of the shares, or that all the shares are to be without par value`)
             ELSE (    stock's `the certificate states the total number of shares of stock which the corporation has authority to issue`
                   AND stock's `the certificate states the number of shares of each class`
                   AND stock's `the certificate specifies each class the shares of which are to be without par value, each class the shares of which are to have par value, and the par value of the shares of each class with par value`))
        AND ((NOT (stock's `the incorporators desire to fix by the certificate the designations, powers, preferences and rights, and qualifications, limitations or restrictions, permitted by § 151 for a class or series`))
             OR stock's `the certificate sets forth a statement of them`)
        AND ((NOT (stock's `the incorporators desire to grant the board of directors authority to fix by resolution any of them not fixed by the certificate`))
             OR stock's `the certificate sets forth an express grant of that authority`))

-- A nonstock corporation: the stock provisions do not apply; the certificate states that the corporation is not
-- authorized to issue capital stock, and the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership or
-- other criteria for identifying members.
-- src:45 | The foregoing provisions of this paragraph shall not apply to nonstock corporations. In the case of nonstock corporations, the fact that they are not authorized to issue capital stock shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation. The conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members, of nonstock corporations shall likewise be stated in the certificate of incorporation or …
-- src:45 | In the case of nonstock corporations, the fact that they are not authorized to issue capital stock shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation. The conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members, of nonstock corporations shall likewise be stated in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
DECLARE `s 102(a)(4) Nonstock corporation stated` HAS
    `the certificate states that the corporation is not authorized to issue capital stock`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:45 | The foregoing provisions of this paragraph shall not apply to nonstock corporations. In the case of nonstock corporations, the fact that they are not authorized to issue capital stock shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation. The conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members, of nonstock corporations shall likewise be stated in the certificate of incorporation or …
-- src:45 | In the case of nonstock corporations, the fact that they are not authorized to issue capital stock shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation. The conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members, of nonstock corporations shall likewise be stated in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
GIVEN stated IS A `s 102(a)(4) Nonstock corporation stated`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(4) the certificate and the bylaws set forth what a nonstock corporation must state` stated MEANS
        stated's `the certificate states that the corporation is not authorized to issue capital stock`
    AND stated's `the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members`

-- Which of the two sets of requirements governs depends on the kind of corporation.
-- src:45 | The foregoing provisions of this paragraph shall not apply to nonstock corporations. In the case of nonstock corporations, the fact that they are not authorized to issue capital stock shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation. The conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members, of nonstock corporations shall likewise be stated in the certificate of incorporation or …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      stock IS A `s 102(a)(4) Authorized stock stated`
      nonstock IS A `s 102(a)(4) Nonstock corporation stated`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(4) the certificate and the bylaws set forth what paragraph (a)(4) requires` kind stock nonstock MEANS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
    THEN JUST (`s 102(a)(4) the certificate and the bylaws set forth what a nonstock corporation must state` nonstock)
    ELSE `s 102(a)(4) the certificate sets forth the authorized stock` stock

-- Members of a nonstock corporation. Nonstock corporations shall have members, but the want of members does not
-- affect otherwise valid corporate acts or work a forfeiture or dissolution. If neither the certificate nor the
-- bylaws state the criteria, the members are those entitled to vote for the election of the members of the
-- governing body under the certificate or bylaws or otherwise, until the certificate or bylaws provide otherwise.
-- src:45 | If neither the certificate of incorporation nor the bylaws of a nonstock corporation state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members, the members of the corporation shall be deemed to be those entitled to vote for the election of the members of the governing body pursuant to the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of such corporation or otherwise until thereafter otherwise provided by the certificate of incorporation or the …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
GIVEN `the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the stated conditions or criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to vote for the election of the members of the governing body pursuant to the certificate or bylaws or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(4) the person is a member of the nonstock corporation` `the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members` `the person meets the stated conditions or criteria` `the person is entitled to vote for the election of the members of the governing body pursuant to the certificate or bylaws or otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members`
    THEN `the person meets the stated conditions or criteria`
    ELSE `the person is entitled to vote for the election of the members of the governing body pursuant to the certificate or bylaws or otherwise`

