`s 102(a)(4) the nonstock corporation has forfeited its existence or is dissolved because it has no members` MEANS FALSE

-- Classes or groups of members, the future creation of further classes (including senior ones), full, limited or
-- no voting rights (including a vote on a specified transaction without a vote for the governing body), and
-- voting on any basis: a nonstock corporation may provide for each, in the certificate or the bylaws. The grant of
-- voting rights is "except as otherwise provided in this chapter".
-- src:45 | Nonstock corporations may provide for classes or groups of members having relative rights, powers and duties, and may make provision for the future creation of additional classes or groups of members having such relative rights, powers and duties as may from time to time be established, including rights, powers and duties senior to existing classes and groups of members. …
-- src:45 | Except as otherwise provided in this chapter, nonstock corporations may also provide that any member or class or group of members shall have full, limited, or no voting rights or powers, including that any member or class or group of members shall have the right to vote on a specified transaction even if that member or class or group of members does not have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation. Voting by members of a nonstock corporation may be on a per capita, number, financial interest, class, group, or any other basis set forth. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
DECLARE `s 102(a)(4) Provision for members` IS ONE OF
    `classes or groups of members having relative rights, powers and duties`
    `provision for the future creation of additional classes or groups of members, including ones senior to existing classes and groups`
    `full, limited or no voting rights or powers for a member or class or group of members`
    `the right to vote on a specified transaction without the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body`
    `voting by members on a per capita, number, financial interest, class, group or any other basis`

-- src:45 | Nonstock corporations may provide for classes or groups of members having relative rights, powers and duties, and may make provision for the future creation of additional classes or groups of members having such relative rights, powers and duties as may from time to time be established, including rights, powers and duties senior to existing classes and groups of members. …
-- src:45 | Except as otherwise provided in this chapter, nonstock corporations may also provide that any member or class or group of members shall have full, limited, or no voting rights or powers, including that any member or class or group of members shall have the right to vote on a specified transaction even if that member or class or group of members does not have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation. Voting by members of a nonstock corporation may be on a per capita, number, financial interest, class, group, or any other basis set forth. …
-- src:45 | The provisions referred to in the 3 preceding sentences may be set forth in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(a)(4) (src:45)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      provision IS A `s 102(a)(4) Provision for members`
      `this chapter otherwise provides for the voting provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is set forth in the certificate or the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(a)(4) the nonstock corporation may make the provision for its members` kind provision `this chapter otherwise provides for the voting provision` `the provision is set forth in the certificate or the bylaws` MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
    AND `the provision is set forth in the certificate or the bylaws`
    AND (CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `classes or groups of members having relative rights, powers and duties` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `provision for the future creation of additional classes or groups of members, including ones senior to existing classes and groups` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `full, limited or no voting rights or powers for a member or class or group of members` THEN NOT (`this chapter otherwise provides for the voting provision`)
         WHEN `the right to vote on a specified transaction without the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body` THEN NOT (`this chapter otherwise provides for the voting provision`)
         WHEN `voting by members on a per capita, number, financial interest, class, group or any other basis` THEN TRUE)

§§ `s 102(a)(5) and (6) The incorporators and the first directors`

